<https://www.gov.uk/government/history/past-prime-ministers/william-pitt> <http://schema.org/description> "At just 24 years old, William Pitt The Younger, son of Pitt the Elder , was the youngest Prime Minister in history. He died aged only 46. He was exhausted by the demands of an office whose modern conception he helped to establish, and of a peculiarly threatening international situation which frustrated many of his political goals."@en <https://www.gov.uk/government/history/past-prime-ministers/william-pitt> .
