<https://www.gov.uk/government/history/past-prime-ministers/william-bentinck-duke-of-portland> <http://schema.org/description> "The Duke of Portland always thought of himself as a Whig. However he was an important figure in a realignment of British politics which laid the foundation of Tory government in the early nineteenth century. This gave him a significance far greater than his 2 brief spells as prime minister would suggest."@en <https://www.gov.uk/government/history/past-prime-ministers/william-bentinck-duke-of-portland> .
